      "stageRecord": "Each VP combines with an abstract past-tense I⁰ to form I′, and its subject occupies Spec-IP. This adopts the GB implementation in which external arguments are introduced in Spec-IP, rather than first occupying a VP-internal position; consequently, no subject movement or subject trace is required. The VP assigns the Agent role to its subject through predication, and finite I licenses nominative Case. For the first conjunct, a lexicalist treatment of inflection licenses the already inflected verb revised through its local tense relationship with abstract I; neither V-to-I movement nor affix lowering is posited. The second I carries past tense but still lacks an overt exponent. Its reconstructed verb remains in the base form because the eventual finite exponent will be auxiliary did.",
