      "stageRecord": "Too projects AdvP and right-adjoins to the second I′, outside the VP-deletion domain. This attachment lets too modify the surviving predication while remaining pronounced after did. Its additive interpretation associates Felix with the alternative subject Nora: the antecedent establishes that Nora revised the article, and the second clause asserts that Felix did so as well. The two finite IPs then form a binary X-bar coordination headed by and, with the first IP in the specifier position of ConjP and the second as the complement of Conj⁰. No CP layer, wh-movement, or A′-dependency is required for these coordinated declaratives. The completed structure pronounces exactly the supplied tokens; the reconstructed VP remains syntactically present but silent.",
